-- title:
--   Separability of the level-H q-expansion field over κ(̄ j,̄ j_{M'})
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\kappa$ be any field of characteristic $q$ (not assumed perfect, finite, or algebraically closed). Work inside the Laurent series field $\kappa((X))$. Two intermediate fields of $\kappa((X))$ over $\kappa$ are involved. The smaller, [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L61), is generated over $\kappa$ by the two series `jqModC κ` $= X^{-1}\cdot \overline{\mathrm{jNum}}$, the coefficientwise reduction to $\kappa$ of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$, and `jqNModC κ M'`, its image under the substitution `qExpand κ M'` raising the variable to the $M'$-th power; thus it is $\kappa(\bar j,\bar j(q^{M'}))$. The larger, [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L76), is generated over $\kappa$ by the family [`ModularCurve.intFormRatiosC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L83) attached to the congruence subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), namely the image in $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the subgroup of $\Gamma_0(q^2M')$ whose associated unit in $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}$ lies in `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$. The assertion is that every element $x$ of this larger field is separable over the smaller one, i.e. $x$ is algebraic over $\kappa(\bar j,\bar j(q^{M'}))$ with separable minimal polynomial. No inclusion between the two fields is asserted; separability is stated elementwise for the subfield of $\kappa((X))$ generated by $\kappa$ and the two $j$-series.
--
--   This is the separability half of Igusa's description of the reduction modulo $q$ of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ at the Igusa (supersingular/ordinary) level structure, in the $q$-expansion formulation: the level-$H$ $q$-expansion field is separable over the field generated by the reduced $j$-series of levels $1$ and $M'$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isLocalHom_and_isSeparable_residueField_of_eq_comap_gauss_of_levelH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isLocalHom_and_isSeparable_residueField_of_eq_comap_gauss_of_levelH), where the residue field of the Gauss valuation at $\infty$ is identified and its separability over the base is needed; its proof quotes the Kummer-generator description of the Igusa function field together with the existence of a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $q$ and the algebraicity of its residue field over $\mathbb{F}_q$.
